<article class="env-lemma" id="06DQ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06DQ">Lemma <span data-tag="06DQ">74.9.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. Let $x \in |X|$. If $f$ is flat at $x$ and $X$ is geometrically unibranch at $x$, then $Y$ is geometrically unibranch at $f(x)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Consider the map of étale local rings $\mathcal{O}_{Y, f(\overline{x})} \to \mathcal{O}_{X, \overline{x}}$. By Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/04NG" data-tag="04NG">67.30.8</a> this is flat. Hence if $\mathcal{O}_{X, \overline{x}}$ has a unique minimal prime, so does $\mathcal{O}_{Y, f(\overline{x})}$ (by going down, see Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00HS" data-tag="00HS">10.39.19</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>